abstract: "A public release of Finite Contact Theory, a long-range finite reconstruction program. This v0.2 chapter defines a behavior-conditioned contextual capacity (the least operator-norm capacity any sharp quantum model must carry to reproduce a fixed exclusivity-graph behavior) and proves an exact strict preparation gap at KCBS-pentagon scope, hand-checkable in rational arithmetic by a shipped dependency-free script; the v0.1 binary-Bell quantum-boundary chapter is unchanged, and every unearned generalization is held open by name."
